<title>USA: Eagle-Picher disclosure statement OKd.</title>
<headline>Eagle-Picher disclosure statement OKd.</headline>
<dateline>CINCINNATI 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eagle-Picher Industries said Wednesday it has received approval for an amended bankruptcy plan and disclosure statement, pegging the liability for settling asbestos-related personal injury claims at $2 billion.</p>
<p>The U.S. Bankruptcy Court of Cincinnati approved the disclosure statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>If the new plan becomes effective, the previous $2.5 billion estimated liability for current and future claims, which had been estimated by the bankruptcy court, would be dismissed, the company said.</p>
</text>
